WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.375
A tiny open

00:00:01.187 --> 00:00:02.614
model matched frontier

00:00:02.425 --> 00:00:03.934
APIs at Airbnb

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:05.802
Airbnb Engineering

00:00:05.614 --> 00:00:06.816
fine-tuned Google's

00:00:06.663 --> 00:00:07.854
small Gemma 4

00:00:07.689 --> 00:00:09.104
E2B model for

00:00:08.916 --> 00:00:10.425
policy classification

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:11.203
served on a

00:00:11.015 --> 00:00:12.783
single NVIDIA RTX

00:00:12.595 --> 00:00:13.880
Pro 6000

00:00:14.398 --> 00:00:15.671
Its max F1

00:00:15.483 --> 00:00:16.544
score jumped from

00:00:16.356 --> 00:00:19.728
0.563 to 0.902

00:00:19.917 --> 00:00:20.730
on par with

00:00:20.542 --> 00:00:21.567
the best frontier

00:00:21.379 --> 00:00:22.169
APIs

00:00:22.308 --> 00:00:23.416
That's open weights

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:24.713
plus careful fine-tuning

00:00:25.238 --> 00:00:26.570
Median latency was

00:00:26.382 --> 00:00:28.103
just 35 milliseconds

00:00:27.915 --> 00:00:29.565
versus about 900

00:00:29.377 --> 00:00:30.391
for the APIs

00:00:30.521 --> 00:00:31.511
at roughly one

00:00:31.323 --> 00:00:32.018
percent of the

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:32.455
cost

00:00:32.561 --> 00:00:33.822
on one GPU

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:35.364
Full story on

00:00:35.175 --> 00:00:36.071
the dashboard
